# A change to a workflow can touch anything: the workflow runs with the
# repository token, on a non-ephemeral self-hosted runner that also hosts the
# workspace daemon. The same goes for the deployment manifests and for the
# proxy, which is the only place that sees the providers' keys.
#
# A `CODEOWNERS` file blocks nothing on its own: GitHub only enforces it as a
# required review when the protected branch has the "Require review from Code
# Owners" option turned on. Still pending in #182.

*                                   @careb36

/.github/                           @careb36
/.github/workflows/                 @careb36
/.github/dependabot.yml             @careb36
/deployment/                        @careb36
/db/                                @careb36
/llm-proxy/                         @careb36
/vscode-daemon/                     @careb36
/scripts/e2e/                       @careb36

# The policy and secrets files: a change here rewrites what counts as
# evidence and which keys get in.
/backend/app/services/verification.py  @careb36
/backend/app/services/board.py         @careb36
/backend/app/routers/auth.py           @careb36
/backend/app/config.py                     @careb36
/.env.example                          @careb36
/SECURITY.md                           @careb36
